s price a Democratic win at 93-95%", "Sparse polling still shows Haaland leading by high single digits on average", "Open seat in a D+4 state; Haaland's refusal to debate is the main lingering risk"], "rationale": "Haaland's lopsided fundraising advantage, New Mexico's Democratic lean, and uniformly favorable expert ratings and market prices point to a clear Democratic win; the limited polling, averaging a high-single-digit lead, supports a margin near ten points.", "watch": "Fresh polling showing the lead slipping into the low single digits, or sustained backlash over Haaland skipping debates, would signal a tightening race.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Michelle Lujan Grisham (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "New Mexico's governor's race is an open-seat contest between Democrat Deb Haaland and Republican Gregg Hull, with term-limited incumbent Michelle Lujan Grisham not on the ballot. The state leans Democratic by about four points, and Haaland holds an enormous financial advantage, having raised roughly $11 million to Hull's under half a million. Expert race ratings uniformly place the contest in the Solid or Likely Democratic column, and betting markets price her chances in the mid-90s.\n\nPolling has been sparse, but available surveys show Haaland ahead by margins from one to seventeen points, averaging around eight. The most visible controversy has been the failure to agree on any debate, with Haaland ending talks and drawing criticism that skipping debates risks voter trust. Even so, the combination of money, state lean, and outside assessments points to a comfortable but not guaranteed Democratic win.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9664, "margin": 10.58}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9571, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9605, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.948, "margin": 10.2}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9415, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9502, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9552, "margin": 10.0}]}